ONVIF device identity from the environment for go2rtc v1.9.15 (7c05066), applied after
onvif-profile.patch (it changes lines next to that patch's). Upstream announces itself as
go2rtc to every client: GetDeviceInformation answers Model go2rtc with no Manufacturer, and
GetScopes holds onvif://www.onvif.org/name/go2rtc and location/github, so UniFi Protect named
every copy "go2rtc". ONVIF_NAME, ONVIF_MANUFACTURER and ONVIF_MODEL replace those values when
set and not empty; ONVIF_LOCATION replaces the location, and set to "" drops that scope. Scope
values are URL-escaped (url.PathEscape), and every GetDeviceInformation field is XML-escaped,
the SerialNumber included: it is the request's Host header, which upstream pasted as is. The
SerialNumber itself stays upstream's (the address the client reached, unique per copy, which
Home Assistant needs). Without the env vars, both answers keep upstream's values (GetScopes
byte for byte). Comes with its own tests (go test ./pkg/onvif/ ./internal/onvif/).

